an translations","Terms with Vietnamese translations","en:Happiness","en:Personality"],"id":"9b07d23a-fcac-450d-a4b6-9aab699707f7"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]},"Joyce":{"id":"22684a5b-40f2-492f-9820-5ea05a136a30","word":"Joyce","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"an English and Irish patronymic surname","tags":["feminine"],"word":"Joice"}],"pos":"name","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"The vote was 213-209 along party lines. Republican members of the House Ethics Committee – Michael Guest of Mississippi, Dave Joyce of Ohio, Andrew Garbarino of New York, John Rutherford of Florida and Michelle Fischbach of Minnesota – voted present. GOP Rep. Ken Buck of Colorado also voted present but he is not on the Ethics Committee.","ref":"2023 June 21, Haley Talbot and Kristin Wilson, “House votes to censure Democratic congressman who led Trump investigations”, in CNN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[126,131]],"id":"120ebb94-a3b4-4178-b91f-a6519c9a1cf8"}],"categories":["English surnames","English surnames from patronymics","English terms with quotations"],"links":[["Irish","Irish"],["surname","surname"]],"glosses":["An English and Irish surname originating as a patronymic."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"6e4996f1-ce79-4934-b92a-9b9dd7178bd0"},{"examples":[{"text":"\"It's a curious name,\" remarked Captain Levison. \"Joyce - Joyce! I never heard such a name. Is it a Christian name or a surname?\"\n\"She was baptised Joyce. It is not so very uncommon. Her name is Joyce Hallijohn. She has been with us several years.\"","ref":"1860, Mrs Henry Wood (Ellen Wood), East Lynne:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[50,55],[58,63],[148,153],[195,200]],"id":"cb53230b-cd92-42a1-9585-ea4f338ba748"},{"text":"You call me mother, and I remember my mother again,\nsomewhere in greater Boston, dying.\nI remember we named you Joyce\nso we could call you Joy.","ref":"1959, Anne Sexton, The Double Image:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[112,117]],"id":"f134197e-1938-4406-a4d8-3f93726b685b"}],"categories":["English female given names","English female given names from Celtic languages","English given names","English terms with quotations","Quotation templates to be cleaned"],"links":[["given name","given name"],["folk etymology","folk etymology"],["joy","joy#English"],["rejoice","rejoice#English"]],"glosses":["A female given name from the Celtic languages, associated by folk etymology with joy and rejoice."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"6d9e3ef1-ecb3-4e74-af57-b9c7a4ec2912"},{"categories":["en:Places in Washington, USA","en:Places in the United States","en:Unincorporated communities in Washington, USA"],"links":[["unincorporated community","unincorporated community"],["Clallam County","Clallam County#English"],["Washington","Washington#English"],["United States","United States#English"]],"glosses":["An unincorporated community in Clallam County, Washington, United States, named after founder Joseph M. Joyce."],"tags":["countable","uncountable"],"id":"a0896eec-6e06-4fb6-9ef5-7b5474e737dd"}],"related":[{"word":"Jocelyn"}],"synonyms":[]},"joyride":{"id":"40999118-fbdb-4c74-a49b-e9c1a8aeb1e4","word":"joyride","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"to take a joyride","word":"rolezar"}],"pos":"verb","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"You joyride around for a while listening / to the radio, and then abandon death, walk / away, and leave death for the police / to find.","ref":"c. 1969, Richard Brautigan, Death is a Beautiful Parked Car Only:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[4,11]],"id":"d50d3a77-5325-4a8a-99b6-a5eaf3be71d1"},{"text":"His parents were out shopping and he used the opportunity to snatch the keys to the 1999 Suzuki Esteem and joyride around the neighborhood.","ref":"2008 August 27, Laura Albanese, “Joyriding teen arrested on delinquency charge”, in Newsday, retrieved 25 Sep 2008:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[107,114]],"id":"cc81aa34-3372-40f6-8530-36043ed09328"}],"categories":["English intransitive verbs","English terms with quotations"],"raw_glosses":["(intransitive) To take a joyride."],"glosses":["To take a joyride."],"tags":["intransitive"],"id":"a5b75e41-5764-4606-92d2-d864280411af"}],"related":[{"word":"joyrider"},{"word":"joyriding"}],"synonyms":[]},"Joycean":{"id":"ce9da2f2-f24a-4276-81ab-279087743113","word":"Joycean","trans":[{"lang":"Portuguese","code":"pt","lang_code":"pt","sense":"pertaining to James Joyce or his writings","word":"joyceano"}],"pos":"adj","tags":null,"senses":[{"examples":[{"text":"Even Muldoon's fans find some of the “difficulty” of this pyrotechnical erudition too playful, suspecting him of a Joycean desire to “keep the professors busy”.","ref":"2001 May 12, Robert Potts, “The poet at play”, in The Guardian, →ISSN:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[115,122]],"id":"15093ae1-d7cf-4b73-b97e-59b435121981"},{"text":"Around the world these days there are thousands of Joycean scholars who make their living parsing and reparsing the great man who, perhaps much to his chagrin if he were alive, has become a symbol of all things Irish to millions.","ref":"2011 June 15, Debbie McGoldrick, “The genius of the Irish writer James Joyce”, in IrishCentral.com:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[51,58]],"id":"becc5288-0181-48bc-bbbe-e7e2de206bbf"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations"],"glosses":["Of or pertaining to James Joyce (1882–1941) or his writings."],"id":"616905f4-8fc6-4345-a90c-0e6b1614048a"},{"examples":[{"text":"Jimson is a total nonconformist and his god is William Blake, whom he quotes endlessly in his somewhat Joycean interior monologues.","ref":"1984, Anthony Burgess, “The Horse's Mouth — Joyce Cary [1944]”, in Ninety-nine Novels, London: Allison & Busby:","type":"quotation","bold_text_offsets":[[103,110]],"id":"89ad84f2-7be3-4f1d-82cd-c2fdf05fda37"}],"categories":["English terms with quotations","en:Writing"],"links":[["writing","writing#Noun"],["verbally","verbally"],["inventive","inventive"]],"raw_glosses":["(of writing) In a verbally inventive style similar to that of James Joyce."],"glosses":["In a verbally inventive style similar to that of James Joyce."],"raw_tags":["of writing"],"id":"a5f3e7db-ba77-457f-80b3-ff4d8d9f3993"}],"related":[],"synonyms":[]}}
